{
  "description": "The open bill a reissue starts from (POS spec §18, PRD W5, owner answer 3 to W1-12): the voided sale's tier, its lines (item, quantity, list and floor as they were, the unit price), its bill discount, and its price approvals (below_list, below_floor, on a line or on the bill discount) as they were, so they hold while the prices stay (POS spec §10). Credit approvals are never kept on an open bill (POS spec §15). The seller is who reissues; the customer and walk-in phone are the counter's to set (not in the domain bill). Whether a unit allows fractions comes from the local catalog; an item no longer there allows them only if its quantity has one. Each new line gets the next of the given ids; a list of ids that doesn't fit the lines is unknown_line. …a1 a salesman, …a2 a manager, …a7 another salesman.",
